From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gianluca Mazza <info@gianlucamazza.it>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:31:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Input: elants_i2c - take the physical size from
 touchscreen-x/y-mm

The resolution reported for the axes is computed from the sensor size
the eKTF firmware returns. On the Nexus 7 2013 (eKTF3624, axes swapped
with touchscreen-swapped-x-y) this gives 18 and 6 units/mm, i.e. a
75 x 373 mm touchscreen for a 94 x 151 mm panel, which throws off every
millimetre based threshold in userspace.

Use the generic touchscreen-x-mm and touchscreen-y-mm properties when
the board provides them; they describe the reported axes, so no
swapping is needed. Fall back to the firmware values otherwise.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/elants_i2c.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/elants_i2c.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/elants_i2c.c
index 17175adca..6ae255ec7 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/elants_i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/elants_i2c.c
@@ -1394,6 +1394,7 @@ static bool elants_acpi_is_hid_device(struct device *dev)
 
 static int elants_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 {
+	u32 x_mm, y_mm;
 	union i2c_smbus_data dummy;
 	struct elants_data *ts;
 	unsigned long irqflags;
@@ -1493,7 +1494,20 @@ static int elants_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 
 	touchscreen_parse_properties(ts->input, true, &ts->prop);
 
-	if (ts->chip_id == EKTF3624 && ts->phy_x && ts->phy_y) {
+	if (!device_property_read_u32(&client->dev, "touchscreen-x-mm", &x_mm) &&
+	    !device_property_read_u32(&client->dev, "touchscreen-y-mm", &y_mm) &&
+	    x_mm && y_mm) {
+		/*
+		 * The board knows the physical size better than the firmware.
+		 * The properties describe the reported axes, while prop.max_x
+		 * and prop.max_y stay in the sensor orientation.
+		 */
+		u32 rx = ts->prop.swap_x_y ? ts->prop.max_y : ts->prop.max_x;
+		u32 ry = ts->prop.swap_x_y ? ts->prop.max_x : ts->prop.max_y;
+
+		ts->x_res = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(rx + 1, x_mm);
+		ts->y_res = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(ry + 1, y_mm);
+	} else if (ts->chip_id == EKTF3624 && ts->phy_x && ts->phy_y) {
 		/* calculate resolution from size */
 		ts->x_res = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(ts->prop.max_x, ts->phy_x);
 		ts->y_res = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(ts->prop.max_y, ts->phy_y);
